## 1. High-Level System Architecture

RenoGo is a single-page web application (SPA) created using:
- **Build Tool**: Vite (with `@vitejs/plugin-react`)
- **UI Library**: React 19 + React DOM 19
- **Language**: TypeScript with strict typing
- **Routing**: React Router DOM (v7)
- **UI Frameworks**: Material-UI (MUI core `@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, `@mui/x-charts`) & custom CSS stylesheets
- **Mock REST API**: `json-server` (running on port `5000`) with Vite reverse proxying `/api/*` to `http://localhost:5000/*`

### Network & Proxy Flow:
```
Browser (React Frontend at http://localhost:5173)
       │
       ▼ (calls fetch('/api/orders') or fetch('/api/dealers'))
Vite Dev Server (vite.config.ts Proxy)
       │
       │ rewrites path: /api/orders  ──►  /orders
       ▼
json-server (running on port 5000 from backend/db.json)
```

---

## 2. Role-Based Workflow & End-to-End Request Lifecycle

The application orchestrates a 6-tier supply chain:

```
[1. Dealer]
    └── Creates Fleet Request (e.g., 50 Kiger units)
           │
           ▼
[2. Manufacturer]
    └── Reviews Request, maps physical inventory, splits between:
        - "Available" (in warehouse)
        - "To Manufacture" (needs factory production)
           │
           ▼
[3. Supervisor]
    └── Reviews allocated request, configures Quotation, GST,
        advance deposit %, and Manufacturer Bank Details.
           │
           ▼
[4. Sales Manager]
    └── Verifies the entire order & financial quote;
        Approves or Declines with notes.
           │
           ▼
[5. Dealer Manager]
    └── Receives approved request, acknowledges terms,
        views bank details, and submits payment proof.
           │
           ▼
[6. Admin]
    └── High-level system overview: dealer network, user management,
        catalog tracking, and production stage tracking.
```

---

